# Build output. `tsc` emits here, and committing emitted JavaScript beside its TypeScript is how
# this repository once made every model unimportable in tests - a stale `.js` that the test runner
# resolved in preference to the `.ts`.
dist/

# Probe harness logs. Written by tools/probe-*.ps1 through a redirect, because the harness reports
# through Write-Host and a filtered pipeline shows nothing while the probes run normally.
tools/.probe-*.log
tools/.probe-*.err

# Smoke-run logs. `tools/smoke-play.ts` prints a launch token, so these must never be committed
# even though the round it belongs to lives in an in-memory database that dies with the process.
tools/.smoke*.log
tools/.smoke*.err

# Local secrets. The service refuses to boot without them, so there will be a file like this.
.env
.env.local

# The template is `env.example`, with NO LEADING DOT, and renaming it to `.env.example` for
# convention's sake would delete it from the repository without saying so: the root .gitignore
# ignores `.env*`, so the file would simply stop being committed and the next deployment would
# have no documentation of the variables it needs. `deploy/env.example` is named the same way,
# for the same reason.
